       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. A 2,000 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Even with normal liver and kidney function, that exposes the patient to a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options that stay within standard limits:\n- **1,000 mg by mouth three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **1,000 mg by mouth four times daily**, which is 4,000 mg/day. This is the usual ceiling. Some institutions use a lower cap, such as 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n\nDid you mean one of these, for example 1,000 mg instead of 2,000 mg? If you do want the 2,000 mg dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. Otherwise, tell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away."
